[{"id":"VRCE-6-22-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":1,"english":"Then the spies of the king informed him of the forces of Rāghava, incapable of being agitated, which had stationed themselves on Suvela. Hearing the arrival of Rāma's mighty army from the spies, Ravana was a little agitated, and he spoke to the ministers.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9e3f6dfa3cdde24f55964d4744bf526d523f1243fea5518b5c192cc513e12ce3","compact":"b60d6333eef679f56aef93479a57b760827800808af9f7e0ece083be30495c96","nasal":"5c1043bf286cae3e31e453aa0b71f2218d85f2ef09fff6fb4d81fa90f6956bcc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":2,"english":"Then the spies of the king informed him of the forces of Rāghava, incapable of being agitated, which had stationed themselves on Suvela. Hearing the arrival of Rāma's mighty army from the spies, Ravana was a little agitated, and he spoke to the ministers.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.722,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9bedcf8c6b2ecea98379b12c8c37ead5c18aab1d9e0f7b78d15469cab60f743","compact":"1fd155b76a6bc3ba12fa006618825cdf49bc79e86cede558e84b880fd607231b","nasal":"1fd155b76a6bc3ba12fa006618825cdf49bc79e86cede558e84b880fd607231b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":3,"english":"Let the ministers speedily present themselves, having their wits about them, the time forsooth has come for counsel.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2c60ce80658bb9e7383563a37b5d1652c8ea4c35da569b37f6d07ce4efcb4b6b","compact":"fe90c1c4a716499b410b0ac18a67299d1697095a1645d8da752b34037f660477","nasal":"ea9133b5ab23368a7f05b01c6a038293bced5a54981866f8b11aadef5cbf77ff"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":4,"english":"Hearing his mandate, those Raksasas, his counsellors, swiftly presented themselves. And then he consulted with his Rākşasa counsellors.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.691,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"46e747f49b6364599ccec7e197421e00b7089b09365118f015223574aa5010d2","compact":"162949005ac87af4d15380deb55b810e2cf6bcfe6449963d3ec98ab3f7fef217","nasal":"c3bbe475bf897bb0bd9f3846de36969a21dcc57c3db8bd99cb1a25ed914a6a75"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":5,"english":"Having deliberated duly, that resistless one, dismissing his ministers, entered his own abode.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b0cd81b72e042b056dedd9c6f31a3f9d46963dd7e8fd0699462a59e780884096","compact":"6d389980bac5878905107a95aa33faea750d1ef00728de8923753853467fc3d2","nasal":"6fb0696856d41b4e9b964d71d67b836406a1762bd3f089a46688ada3df6ce362"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":6,"english":"Then, taking with him the highly strong Vidyujjihva, huge bodied and gifted with the powers of illusion, he entered where Mithila's daughter was.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.468,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"05b93f999f838ef4267936e1439d65537e9c3c7f60494008dd2c350d015b7389","compact":"046f8e4ebba5008f07885f088c9f5cd58b737ea8220911751e95a131d3706d5c","nasal":"4ad47b79b23f501296e5f74bbf48346614a7a6c1af5ffa0fa3801bccd8461c7d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":7,"english":"The lord of Rākşasas said to Vidyujjihva, skilled in illusion, Do you bring Janaka's daughter under the sway of illusion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.731,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74bd09a421ca7ea771dba296d285f42edac06fab1fd34dba5887a421a95667c8","compact":"05b0524290c7a111243ad7e8ea802d973cc88a0a823307ca9beab5c020ebd458","nasal":"05b0524290c7a111243ad7e8ea802d973cc88a0a823307ca9beab5c020ebd458"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":8,"english":"O ranger of the night, do you, taking an illusory head of Rāghava, as well as a mighty bow with the shaft (set), present yourself before me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ef7af72e204a618d942839589e3d7d78f1350db138b509e5c339f7178de4c52","compact":"0fdcf0d28a444af7e86c03402756e3ffa5bdc60293b537b7fec9cd4d37b7f402","nasal":"0fdcf0d28a444af7e86c03402756e3ffa5bdc60293b537b7fec9cd4d37b7f402"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":9,"english":"Thus accosted, the night-ranger, Vidyujjibha, saying, So be it, displayed that desired illusion to Ravana. Thereat, the king, eager to meet with Sītā in the Asoka woods, well-pleased, conferred an excellent ornament on him.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.484,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-8","DUTT-6-31-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ee3fa798ffd8b3cb912121aaa2c971883b86aea189b1cead262599c485b7db9c","compact":"1eb145768f837f4f5a67b2e5812cc184c203bebff2825746d5af376b28e084ae","nasal":"1eb145768f837f4f5a67b2e5812cc184c203bebff2825746d5af376b28e084ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":10,"english":"Then the exceedingly powerful lord of the Naiſtas, the younger brother of the Dispenser of riches, entered (into that place) and saw (there Sitā) distressed, albeit unworthy of distress, with her head hung down, overwhelmed with woe, sitting on the ground, staying at the aśoka woods, engaged in the contemplation of her lord, conciliated by dreadful Räkşasis remaining near. then, drawing near Sita, Ravana, proclaiming his exultation, said these haughty words to the daughter of Janaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.506,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4a40708938cb33297f16f8dec3e0279c37d33c0157553bea18a9a996cb45d118","compact":"8da2b766fe9db137ac4082fb4cf893c7dc701be7e62a2f2e43ba2025a66e25cb","nasal":"8da2b766fe9db137ac4082fb4cf893c7dc701be7e62a2f2e43ba2025a66e25cb"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":11,"english":"Then the exceedingly powerful lord of the Naiſtas, the younger brother of the Dispenser of riches, entered (into that place) and saw (there Sitā) distressed, albeit unworthy of distress, with her head hung down, overwhelmed with woe, sitting on the ground, staying at the aśoka woods, engaged in the contemplation of her lord, conciliated by dreadful Räkşasis remaining near. then, drawing near Sita, Ravana, proclaiming his exultation, said these haughty words to the daughter of Janaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.759,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3e81867e92c05f729365fcf60b82bb08c6f7ce31ca7d890a6c85e8b96659fd42","compact":"92094639a5efe4b0cc798903745db448a98b76dc3d12e6e436007acdc5ae8ee2","nasal":"6c3227995d648aa1b21a19b9cc683da30e5343fe8f9ac92bde7429abf7056946"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":12,"english":"Then the exceedingly powerful lord of the Naiſtas, the younger brother of the Dispenser of riches, entered (into that place) and saw (there Sitā) distressed, albeit unworthy of distress, with her head hung down, overwhelmed with woe, sitting on the ground, staying at the aśoka woods, engaged in the contemplation of her lord, conciliated by dreadful Räkşasis remaining near. then, drawing near Sita, Ravana, proclaiming his exultation, said these haughty words to the daughter of Janaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3b48efde2fea4999aa5262d22ac02d7c48e71a3fb36809f4f8ac5a5500581593","compact":"2bc6b457260759e4c3d688283376629a515d0c285c90453b0aabb89bc901cd74","nasal":"fec6c14ae5d990f635234a3236e4ed20a14165432e2d4fe3308d55e6e36b3a56"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":13,"english":"O gentle one, he depending on whom you, being soothed by (me), slight me-that slayer of Khara, your husband, Rāghava, has fallen in battle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.542,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65306d05a6f6ffdcc4867937fcea70a14d2741b4f82093dec48ed065a8c7cda6","compact":"f56a0f0f753b467d2406b278f1146301ed4df7994d1587131864df1ad3ba1744","nasal":"1cb785f9525ff1502b7deb9beb98a093dbbc3cb7729b16a456fe0027a40d64dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":14,"english":"Your roots have been completely severed, and your pride has been destroyed by me. In consequence of this calamity, O Sītā, you shall become my wife. O foolish (girl), renounce this idea. What will you do with that is dead?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.667,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a57b24e31f857ba3b2929c5c3eb8f6905fafe7649663e2ce50bc9597a148fe36","compact":"a98897da8a7b45a30724e031e8e081b3b43ecc7535cd42ef6d813659ebc3c88c","nasal":"530785f33a7a36c725446d64b43d7c0ec099d00c8e668ece8994f2a195f9d2f1"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-22-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":22,"verse":15,"english":"O meek (wench), be you the mistress of all my wives. O you of slender religious merit! O you whose object has been defeated! O you that presumes to be wise! Hearken to the destruction of your lord, like the dreadful destruction of Vrtra!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-31-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6022015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f71c0dedb698f8fb85cb4756de6f69f6570b7c32d071d8a902c27d4e4488365","compact":"deffeeba90c